@startuml
title v0001-executor-docker - per-task lifecycle (MVP)

start
:Executor list: GET /v1/tasks?filter=openhands from mocked Router;
if (queued matching task and capacity free?) then (yes)
  :Start per-task OpenHands container;
  :Submit task to that container's OpenHands REST API;
  :Append task.started and task.start_message to State Registry;
  :OpenHands runs agent (LLM, tools, etc.);
  while (task in flight?) is (yes)
    :OpenHands emits message/event;
    :Executor forwards each intermediate message/event to mocked State Registry (POST /v1/tasks/{task_id}/events);
    :Executor refreshes Router task list;
    if (pending_actions include interrupt_task or append_task_message?) then (yes)
      :Executor journals cancel/message action and forwards it to OpenHands;
    else (no)
    endif
  endwhile (terminal status reached)
  :Executor appends task.finished or task.failed to mocked State Registry;
else (no task or capacity full)
  :sleep, return to poll;
endif

stop

@enduml
